were created in the 1970s, when various companies were obliged to issue the nonvoting shares to their workers. \par \par \uc2  Financial holding company Credicorp Ltd. rose 3.7% to end at $10.27. \par \par \uc2  Telefonica SA rose 0.4% to end at $29.50, as the local traded American Depositary Receipts rose to catch up with earlier increases in the share that trades elsewhere. \par \par \uc2  Southern Peru Copper Corp. went the other way, closing down 2.8% at $14.48 on weaker copper prices. \par \par \uc2  -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030403dz4300c1n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
