\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Stock Market And Sol Continue To Strengthen \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2003\par 23:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's sol ended stronger Wednesday in extremely high volumes, despite a fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which purchased $20 million, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $206.2 million so far this year. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4717 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4714-PEN3.4720 to the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed the day before at a midrate of PEN3.4743 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4740-PEN3.4745 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that demand for soles continued rising from companies needing to pay annual income taxes. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN150 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average rate of 3.90%. \par \par \uc2  Another PEN105 million in certificates of deposit also matured Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.90% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes closed sharply higher Wednesday in line with stock markets elsewhere. \par \par \uc2  Lima's broad General Index closed 24.56 points, or 1.57%, stronger at 1586.28. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip Selective Index closed 38.70 points, or 1.59%, higher at 2467.90. \par \par \uc2  Beverage producer Union de Cervecerias Peruanas Backus & Johnston SAA, or Backus, saw its so-called investment share close 5.2% higher at PEN1.43. \par \par \uc2  Colombia's Bavaria SA has launched a public offer for outstanding voting "A" shares of Backus. \par \par \uc2  Investment shares were created in the 1970s, when various companies were obliged to issue the nonvoting shares to their workers. \par \par \uc2  Telefonica SA's rose 3.8% to end at $29.37, following gains in its New York-trade American Depositary Receipts. \par \par \uc2  Banco Wiese Sudameris, the third biggest in Peru, rose 10% to end at PEN0.11. \par \par \uc2  Precious metals miner Buenaventura SAA went the other way, falling 2.3% to end at PEN42.00 on weaker gold prices. \par \par \uc2  -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030402dz420093u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
