\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Stronger; Stock Market Ends Down \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2003\par 22:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's sol ended slightly stronger Friday in low-volume trading, shrugging off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  that bought $8.2 million, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4800 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4798-PEN3.4801 to the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sol had closed the day before at a midrate of PEN3.4803 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4800-PEN3.4805 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN190 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average rate of 3.82%%. \par \par \uc2  The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.80% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Lima's stock indexes closed weaker Friday as Buenaventura SAA and Banco Wiese Sudameris both fell. \par \par \uc2  Lima's broad General Index closed 2.69 points, or 0.17%, lower at 1546.66. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip Selective Index closed 6.78 points, or 0.28%, weaker at 2414.91. \par \par \uc2  Banco Wiese Sudameris, the third-largest bank in the country, fell 10% to end at PEN0.09. \par \par \uc2  The share rose 25% Thursday after Italy's Banca Intesa SpA said earlier this week that it would inject $150 million into the Peruvian bank. \par \par \uc2  Precious metals miner Buenaventura SAA fell 2.0% to end at PEN45.55, partially on weaker gold prices. \par \par \uc2  Telefonica SA's ADR rose 1.7% to end at $29.48, following its New York-traded ADR higher. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221