\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Stronger; Stock Market Ends Down \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2002\par 21:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's sol ended stronger Monday in medium volume trading despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4908 per dollar on  a spread of PEN3.4900-PEN3.4915 per dollar, local traders  said. \par \par \uc2  The sol had closed Friday at a midrate of PEN3.5023 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.5015-PEN3.5030 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $5 million, aiming to offset strong demand from banks and companies for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay end-of-the-year bonuses and taxes. \par \par \uc2  The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars was in April, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said. \par \par \uc2  The sol strengthened to PEN3.4840 at one point in trade Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN40 million in one-year  certificates of deposit at an average rate of 5.02%. \par \par \uc2  Another PEN65 million in certificates of deposit also matured on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.78% on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes closed weaker Monday as zinc miner Volcan and financial holding company Credicorp Ltd both weakened. \par \par \uc2  Lima's broad General Index closed 5.90 points or 0.42%  lower at 1400.80. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip Selective Index closed 13.94 points or 0.63% weaker at 2210.34. \par \par \uc2  Volcan Compania Minera SAA fell 5.9% to end at PEN0.16, on weaker zinc prices. \par \par \uc2  Credicorp Ltd fell 0.8% to end at $9.50. \par \par \uc2  Spain's Telefonica SA went the other direction, rising  1.8% from its close on Friday to end at $27.60 in line with strength in its shares elsewhere. \par \par \uc2  - By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020021216dycg008c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
