\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  cenbank announces new  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  instrument. \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2002\par 23:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments paragraphs 2-3, 5, updates with sol close paragraph 9) \par \par \uc2  LIMA, Peru, July 8 (Reuters) - Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would launch new certificates of deposit based on fluctuating exchange rates as a new instrument to control volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "Without (banks) having to enter the spot dollar market or unload their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions, this new measure ... helps establish a more stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the Bank's General Manager Henry Barclay told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "Without a doubt, it helps eliminate volatility," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement in the official gazette that the certificates would be subject to a readjustment based on the change in the exchange rate registered between the placement and expiry dates. \par \par \uc2  Barclay said the new instruments, to be called readjustable certificates of deposit, could be used from now on when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw fit. Market conditions will determine when they are first used. \par \par \uc2  "The average weighted exchange rates of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted via the system Datatec (a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading system) between 9:30 a.m. and 1:30 p.m. will be used," it said, adding that if that information was not available, an average of the exchange rate published by Reuters would be used. \par \par \uc2  "What makes these certificates in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  different is that they will be readjusted in line with the exchange rate. These \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  will help reduce volatility in the price of the sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar," a banking source who requested anonymity told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically offers certificates of deposit as a liquidity-controlling measure in the financial system. Local banks - Peru has 15 - buy the certificates, meaning there is temporarily less money in circulation, and receive interest on the certificates when they come due." \par \par \uc2  Peru's sol slumped last week against the dollar, closing at its lowest level all year against in a falling market riven by speculation ahead of an expected Cabinet reshuffle this month. The sol closed at 3.5320/3.5335 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020708dy78015o1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
