\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  cenbank announces new  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  instrument. \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2002\par 19:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LIMA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would launch new certificates of deposit based on fluctuating exchange rates as a new instrument to control volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "These certificates will be subject to a readjustment based on the change in the exchange rate registered between the placement and expiry dates," it said in a notice in the official gazette. \par \par \uc2  It did not say when the new instruments, to be called readjustable certificates of deposit, would be launched. \par \par \uc2  "To this end, the average weighted exchange rates of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted via the system Datatec (a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading system) between 9:30 a.m. and 1:30 p.m. will be used," it said. \par \par \uc2  If that information were not available, an average of the exchange rate published by Reuters would be used, it said. \par \par \uc2  "What makes these certificates in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  different is that they will be readjusted in line with the exchange rate. These \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  will help reduce volatility in the price of the sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar," a banking source who requested anonymity told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically offers certificates of deposit as a liquidity-controlling measure in the financial system. Local banks - Peru has 15 - buy the certificates, meaning there is temporarily less money in circulation, and receive interest on the certificates when they come due." \par \par \uc2  Peru's sol slumped last week against the dollar, closing at its lowest level all year against in a falling market riven by speculation ahead of an expected Cabinet reshuffle this month. The sol opened slightly lower at 3.5400/3.5440 against the dollar compared with Friday's close of 3.5400/3.5410. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020708dy7800zco\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
