\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Weaker As Banks,  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buy Dollars \b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2001\par 20:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended weaker Monday in medium volume trade as some banks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought U.S. dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $5.0 million. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4335 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4330-PEN3.4340 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed Friday at a midrate of PEN3.4320 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4315-PEN3.4325 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The sol weakened as there was a light demand for dollars by banks, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased dollars," a trader at Banco de Credito said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $192.0 million so far this year to slow the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including Monday's purchase. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN300 million in overnight repurchase agreements or repos at an average rate of 2.80%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of Dec. 14, the key average overnight lending rate in the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was 3.10%.\par -Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050;\par peru@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011217dxch00aht\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
