\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Weaker As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buy Dollars \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2001\par 20:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended weaker Friday in high volumes as the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market purchasing $5 million, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4320 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4215-PEN3.4225 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed the day before at a midrate of PEN3.4285 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4280-PEN3.4290 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The sol was strong until the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market buying dollars," said a trader at Banco de Credito. \par \par \uc2  The sol strengthened to PEN3.4275 at one point in trading. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $162.0 million so far this year to slow the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including Friday's purchase. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN30 million in one-year certificates of deposits at an average rate of 5.13%. \par \par \uc2  On Friday PEN65 million in certificates of deposit also matured. \par \par \uc2  As of Dec. 6, the key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.94%. \par \par \uc2  -Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011207dxc700a18\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
