\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Gains Respect But Dollar Remains Popular \b0\par\par\uc2  By Virginia Rey-Sanchez \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2001\par 17:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's little-known \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol, is suddenly getting some respect after gaining ground steadily this year against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  That has forced the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars on a regular basis in the last few weeks, aiming to keep the sol from strengthening too fast. \par \par \uc2  The free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has benefited from improved exports, weaker imports and more sol-denominated bond placements. \par \par \uc2  Falling oil prices have left more dollars in Peru, which is a net energy importer. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, lower interest rates have reduced Peru's foreign debt payments, increasing the supply of dollars. An appetite for higher-yielding local instruments has also increased demand for the sol. \par \par \uc2  Still, few expect its recent strength will lead the sol to replace the greenback as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice for everything from real estate to car purchases. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar makes up almost 70% of total banking deposits, and 81.5% of total domestic credits. \par \par \uc2  "There still isn't any process of de-dollarization. The prices of products of high worth are expressed in dollars in the stores," said Juan Carlos Garcia, head of economic analysis with Banco Wiese Sudameris. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We think in dollars. When we stop using the dollar as a reference\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , that's when we start to have a de-dollarization," he added.\par        Pension Funds Buying Debt Instruments\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par So far this year, the sol has appreciated about 2.46% against the U.S.\par dollar, ending Monday at 3.4343 soles per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To keep it from appreciating even more, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been a\par regular buyer of dollars, purchasing $157 million so far this year up to\par Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In 2000 it just bought $3.0 million in total.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials have said they have noted a growing confidence\par in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But, perhaps more importantly, the private pension funds, or AFPs,\par have been buying soles.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "For about the last four months there have been few (private sector)\par fixed income placements and the money that the AFPs have taken in every\par month has been placed with what has been on offer: treasury bonds," said\par Gonzalo Tamayo, head of analysis with consulting firm, Macroconsult.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government has placed PEN1.2 billion in treasury notes on the\par local market this year, aiming to build a yield curve and develop the\par local markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of the end of September, pension fund investments in Peruvian\par treasury bonds tripled to 4.6% of their portfolios from 1.5% in March.\par        Portfolio Shifts Seen As Short-Term Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But fund managers say the portfolio shuffles are likely short-term\par moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the pension funds have invested more in instruments denominated in\par soles it's because there have been more sol placements and not from any\par deliberate decision to change the weight of investments," said Mariano\par Alvarez, chief investment officer for pension fund, Union Vida.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added that a possible default in Argentina could have a knock-on\par effect and "as a long term investor I don't have the luxury of\par drastically changing my portfolio for soles."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Another local fund manager echoed those sentiments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Despite the fact there is no short-term expectations of a\par devaluation, there is always the fear that something will happen locally\par or internationally that would negatively affect the exchange rate," said\par Credifondo investment manager Ignacio Aguirre.\par         Other Factors Weighing Against Sol\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other factors are also weighing against the sol.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists forecast a recovery in the economy next year, which should\par boost imports and cause a drain on U.S. dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moreover, many people have strong memories of hyper-inflation. Price\par increases hit 7,650% in 1990.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Peruvians avoid saving in soles despite the fundamentals that\par indicate there will be no devaluation because hyperinflation left many\par of them deeply traumatized," said Banco Wiese Sudameris' Garcia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speaking to reporters late Monday, the general manager of the Central\par Reserve Bank of Peru, Henry Barclay, said that the trend towards a\par stronger sol could change rapidly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It is going to revert soon. The best way to look at this right now is\par that the net cost of maintaining dollars, which is basically tied to the\par sharp drop in interest rates for dollars. When (interest) rates in soles\par start to fall, this will soon allow for a balance to be found that will\par return us to a more comfortable situation," Barclay said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050;\par peru@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011204dxc40011l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
