\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Weaker On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Dollar Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2001\par 20:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended weaker Monday in medium volumes as the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, buying $12.0 million, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4343 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4340-PEN3.4345 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed Friday at a midrate of PEN3.4325 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4320-PEN3.4330 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The sol was strengthening until the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered in the market, purchasing dollars," a trader at Banco Wiese Sudameris said. \par \par \uc2  The sol strengthened to PEN3.4300 at one point in trading. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $157.0 million so far this year to slow the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN75 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average rate of 3.32%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of Nov. 30, the key average overnight lending rate in the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was 3.43%.\par -Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050;\par peru@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011203dxc300ayj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
