\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Weaker As Ctrl Bk Keeps Buying Dollars \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2001\par 20:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended weaker in medium volume trading Thursday after the fourth consecutive day of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $5 million. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4375 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4370-PEN3.4380 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed the day before at a midrate of PEN3.4368 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4365-PEN3.4370 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Companies were were also in the market buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  "It seemed that there were some companies and banks buying dollars," an analyst said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $130.0 million so far this year, including Thursday's purchases, to slow the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The sol has gained strength as, among other factors, imports have weakened and exports of mining products have increased. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN20 million in overnight repurchase agreements - or repos - at an average rate of 3.41%. \par \par \uc2  As of Nov. 21, the key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.37%. \par \par \uc2  -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011122dxbm0013i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pic