\par\par \b \uc2  REPEAT: Peru's Sol Ends Tad Weaker As Ctrl Bk Buys Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2001\par 23:04\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended slightly weaker Monday after the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bought $9.5 million U.S. dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4410 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4405-PEN3.4415 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed last Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.4400 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4390-PEN3.4410 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was closed on Thursday and Friday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  The sol strengthened to PEN3.4370 at one point in trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The sol was strengthening early in trading but it closed weaker after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased dollars," a trader at Banco de Credito said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $25 million in trade last week, aiming to weaken the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Low interest rates for the U.S. dollar have led to a movement into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN40 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average rate of 4.26%. \par \par \uc2  As of Oct. 31, the key average overnight lending rate was 4.02%, and the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to control the money supply and influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was PEN1.805 billion. \par \par \uc2