\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Stronger Despite Ctrl Bk Dollar Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2001\par 20:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended stronger in high volume trade Monday despite an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $5 million on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4465 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4460-PEN3.4470 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed Friday at a midrate of PEN3.4513 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4510-PEN3.4515 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't able to avoid a strengthening of the sol as its dollar buying was timid," a trader at Banco Wiese Sudameris said. \par \par \uc2  Over the last few weeks the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $29.5 million in an effort to keep the surging sol under control. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN25 million in  six-month certificates of deposit at an average rate of 6.56%. \par \par \uc2  As of October 26, the key average overnight lending rate  was 3.96%, and the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to control the money supply and influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was PEN1.780 billion, unchanged from the day before. \par \par \uc2  -Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011029dxat01y6o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picsc