\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Slightly Weaker; Ctrl Bank Buys Dollars \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2001\par 21:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended slightly weaker Monday in medium volume trading, as the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4508 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4505-PEN3.4510 a dollar. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol had closed Friday at a midrate of PEN3.4500 a dollar on a spread of PEN3.4495-PEN3.4505 a dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $7 million Monday, continuing where it left off last week with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a total of $22.5 million in several days of trading. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the central reserve bank also placed PEN215 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average rate of 3.5%, adding liquidity to the market. \par \par \uc2  BBVA Continental SAB noted Monday that among the reasons for the strength of the sol were expected low demand for U.S. dollars from importers and strong inflows of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to increased mining exports. \par \par \uc2  A treasury bond placement last week on the Lima Stock Exchange also increased demand from institutional investors for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it added. \par \par \uc2  As of Oct. 19, the key average overnight lending rate was 3.71%, while the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to control the money supply and influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was PEN1.930 billion. \par \par \uc2  -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011022dxam0015c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
