\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Weaker As Companies Buy US Dollars \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2001\par 21:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended weaker in medium volume Wednesday as companies bought U.S. dollars, taking advantage of recent strength in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4520 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4515-PEN3.4525 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed the day before at a midrate of PEN3.4485 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.4480-PEN3.4490 per dollar, its strongest level of the year. \par \par \uc2  "Companies purchased dollars for future \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they were cheap," a trader at Banco de Credito said. \par \par \uc2  The sol weakened to PEN3.4555 a dollar at one point in trade. \par \par \uc2  The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in the previous two trading sessions, buying $10 million on Monday and $7.5 million Tuesday in an attempt to keep the sol from strengthening too rapidly. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN90 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average rate of 3.93%. \par \par \uc2  As of Oct. 16, the key average overnight lending rate was 4.61%, and the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to control the money supply and influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was PEN1.930 billion, lower than the day before when it was at PEN2.010 billion. \par \par \uc2  -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011017dxah002qt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
