\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends At Record Low Again Before Vote \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2001\par 21:25\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's nuevo sol ended at another record low on Thursday, but the decline wasn't enough to prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Fears that left-wing presidential candidate Alan Garcia could win Sunday's run-off vote for president have sparked a recent run of selling of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.6310 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.6290-PEN3.6330 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed the day before at a midrate of PEN3.6230 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.6220-PEN3.6240 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Volumes weren't that large," said one market analyst. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell about $12 million to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was the fifth time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it did place PEN30 million in four-week certificates of deposit at an average rate of 15.8%. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight lending rate in soles as of May 30 was 15.59%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of May 30, the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to\par control the money supply and influence the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was PEN1.635\par billion, higher than the previous day's PEN1.610 billion.\par -Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010711dx5v003jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
