\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Sol Ends At Historic Low;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2001\par 21:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nuevo sol ended at an historic low Monday in heavy trading as investors shrugged off U.S. dollar buying by the Central Reserve Bank of Peru. \par \par \uc2  Investors sold soles after new opinion polls showed that former president Alan Garcia was gaining before the June 3 runoff vote for president. \par \par \uc2  Although business professor Alejandro Toledo remains in the lead in new polls, Garcia is closing the gap. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.6130 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.6120-PEN3.6140 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed Friday at a midrate of PEN3.5925 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.5920-PEN3.5930 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There was a heavy level of speculation due to the poll results," a trader at Banco de Credito said. \par \par \uc2  An official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the bank sold about $9 million during two rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The sol weakened to 3.6174 at one point in trading. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  May 9, selling $10 million. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the Central Reserve Bank of Peru placed PEN100 million in 20-week certificates of deposit at an average rate of 13.72%. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight lending rate in soles as of Friday was 9.47%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of Friday, the outstanding value of certificates of deposit, used\par by the government to control the money supply and influence the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was PEN1.465 billion, higher than the day before at PEN1.445\par billion.\par    -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050;\par peru@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx5s02h30\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
