\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Sol Ends Stronger After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2001\par 21:32\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nuevo sol ended stronger Wednesday in high-volume trading after the Central Reserve Bank of Peru sold dollars in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.6083 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.6075-PEN3.6090 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed the previous day at a midrate of PEN3.6093 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.6085-PEN3.6100 per dollar. That was a historic low. \par \par \uc2  The sol weakened to PEN3.617 at one point in the trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The sol strengthened only after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars as banks were buying dollars intensively early in the session," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said commercial banks bought dollars mainly to replace inventories but also for speculation. \par \par \uc2  An official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the institution sold between $9 million to $11 million in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market it sold $26.5 million on April 25 and April 26. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN50 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average rate of 16.30%. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight lending rate in soles as of May 8 was 12.91%. \par \par \uc2  As of May 8, the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to control the money supply and influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was PEN1.745 billion, the same as the day before. \par \par \uc2  -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010711dx59003d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
