\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Sol Ends Weaker Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2001\par 21:50\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nuevo sol ended weaker Thursday despite the second straight day of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it sold dollars to curb a dollar-purchase rally by investors, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The amount of dollars sold Thursday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be announced later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.5925 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.5920-PEN3.5930 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol had closed the day before at a midrate of PEN3.5910 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.5905-PEN3.5915 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Banks bought dollars intensively mainly due to political uncertainty. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sale of dollars couldn't prevent the sol from ending weaker," a trader at Banco Wiese Sudameris said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $17.5 million on Wednesday. The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars was in November 1999. \par \par \uc2  At one point in Thursday's trading, the sol weakened to PEN3.5950. \par \par \uc2  Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been shaken by political uncertainty ahead of a presidential run-off election likely to be held in early June. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN50 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average rate of 11.56%. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight lending rate in soles as of April 25 was 12.19%. \par \par \uc2  As of April 25, the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to control the money supply and influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was PEN1.745 billion, lower than the day before at PEN1.865 billion. \par \par \uc2  -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010711dx4q0039i\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Peru near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50